    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37711" root="لزب" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَبٌ</span></b>  immediately following <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَبٌ</span>, (in the CK,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَرَبٌ</span>,) [meaning a man “ who has no wife, ”] is
an imitative sequent [used by way of pleonasm
and corroboration]. (K.) So likewise <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَزَبَةٌ</span> after
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَبَةٌ</span>. (Ibn-Buzruj.)

